      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-14T11:13:39Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): a vertex within the boundary tolerance of a chord splits it\n\nReview of PR #1651: a vertex split the chord only when the edge\nparameter was within 1e-9 of an end. On a short chamfer edge, a chord\nend that on_boundary accepts (up to 1e-9 mm off the wall) passes the\nvertex by many parameter units, and the gap chord cleared again. Each\nloop vertex within BOUNDARY_TOL mm of the chord line now splits it;\non_boundary and the chord law share that one constant.\n\nPinned by chord_clear::tests::a_chord_end_a_hair_off_the_wall_line_still_splits_at_a_short_chamfer\nand a_vertex_touches_the_chord_within_the_boundary_tolerance_and_not_beyond.\n\nRefs #1620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
